    "Nothing wrong." : {
      "comment" : "Summary of the problem list when there is no error and no warning."
    },
    "Overwritten:" : {
      "comment" : "Heading in the report of a push of screenshots. A list of languages and screenshot names that the push uploaded comes after it."
    },
    "People who already subscribe keep what they pay." : {
      "comment" : "Paragraph in the publish plan under a subscription price, shown as fixed-width text. It says that the price change does not change the price for current subscribers."
    },
    "People who already subscribe move to the new price. On a rise Apple asks them, and cancels the ones who do not answer." : {
      "comment" : "Paragraph in the publish plan under a subscription price, shown as fixed-width text. A rise is a price that goes up. Do not translate Apple."
    },
    "Prices" : {
      "comment" : "Noun. The name of one part of a publish, on its checkbox in the publish sheet and on its report. It is the prices of the in-app purchases."
    },
    "Prices:" : {
      "comment" : "Heading in the publish plan, shown as fixed-width text. A list of price changes comes after it."
    },
    "Privacy Policy URL" : {
      "comment" : "Noun. The name of the privacy policy URL field of the listing. URL is a web address."
    },
    "Product Page Optimization" : {
      "comment" : "Noun. The name of one part of a publish, on its checkbox in the publish sheet and on its report. It is Apple's name for product page tests in App Store Connect."
    },
    "Promotional Text" : {
      "comment" : "Noun. The name of the promotional text field of the listing."
    },
    "Purchasing power" : {
      "comment" : "Noun. The name of a price curve. A price curve is a set of rules that sets a price in each country. This curve sets lower prices in countries with lower income."
    },
    "Push writes over what App Store Connect holds now." : {
      "comment" : "Warning in the publish sheet above the publish button. Push is the action that sends the files to App Store Connect."
    },
    "Raises the price where the tax is high, so that what Apple pays you is about the same everywhere. For per-seat and business pricing." : {
      "comment" : "Description of the Equal proceeds price curve, shown under its name. Per-seat pricing is a price for each user in a company."
    },
    "Read App Store Connect again. A product only has a price ladder once the store knows about it." : {
      "comment" : "Fix in the problem list. A price ladder is the list of fixed prices that the App Store sells in one country. Do not translate App Store Connect."
    },
    "Read App Store Connect first." : {
      "comment" : "Error sentence when a person adds the languages from App Store Connect to the project. The app needs to read App Store Connect before this action."
    },
    "Read App Store Connect with the images, then push them." : {
      "comment" : "Error when a push of images starts from a read that left the images out."
    },
    "Read it, then set status to approved, or ai_approved if a machine wrote it." : {
      "comment" : "Fix in the problem list about a language that is not ready to publish. Do not translate status, approved or ai_approved. They are a JSON key and its values."
    },
    "Read the prices again and write once more. Only what is still wrong goes out." : {
      "comment" : "Line in the report of a push of prices, after a list of prices that App Store Connect refused. Write is the action that sends the prices."
    },
    "Read the resolved prices before pushing. %@" : {
      "comment" : "Fix in the problem list about old price curve data. The value is an English sentence that names the source of the data."
    },
    "Recorded in %@" : {
      "comment" : "Last line in the report of what a push did. The value is the file name of the record of the push."
    },
    "Refused in this state:" : {
      "comment" : "Heading in the report of a push of text. A list of language codes and field names that App Store Connect refused comes after it. The state is the state of the version."
    },
    "Refused:" : {
      "comment" : "Heading in the report of a push of in-app purchases or prices. A list of items that App Store Connect refused comes after it."
    },
    "Remove the folder %@." : {
      "comment" : "How to fix a folder that holds files nothing uses. The value is a folder path."
    },
    "Rename the entry or remove it." : {
      "comment" : "How to fix an entry in poster-frames.json that names a missing file."
    },
    "Rename the file to %@.json, or change productId to %@." : {
      "comment" : "Fix in the problem list. The first value is a product id, used as a file name. The second is the file name without .json. Do not translate productId, which is a JSON key.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
