    "Screenshots copied from an older version folder:" : {
      "comment" : "Heading in the report after the app makes a folder for a new version, shown as fixed-width text. A list of languages and device sizes comes after it."
    },
    "Screenshots copied from another language, as copiesScreenshotsFrom says:" : {
      "comment" : "Heading in the report after the app makes a folder for a new version, shown as fixed-width text. Do not translate copiesScreenshotsFrom. It is a JSON key. A list of languages and device sizes comes after it."
    },
    "Screenshots with no file here. Put the files in these sets before you publish, or App Store Connect loses them:" : {
      "comment" : "Heading in the report after the app makes a folder for a new version, shown as fixed-width text. A list of languages and device sizes comes after it."
    },
    "Screenshots:" : {
      "comment" : "Heading in the publish plan, shown as fixed-width text. A list of screenshot set changes comes after it."
    },
    "Set that country by hand, or leave it out with skip. A year sold with a 12-month commitment needs both prices, and this country's ladder has no instalment Apple would take." : {
      "comment" : "Fix in the problem list about a yearly subscription price paid in 12 monthly instalments. Do not translate skip. It is a JSON key. The ladder is the list of fixed prices in one country."
    },
    "Silenced %lld warnings in %@. They are in %@." : {
      "comment" : "asckit silence --all prints this in the terminal. The count is the number of warnings. The first value is a version, such as 1.0. The second value is a file path, such as versions/1.0/silenced.json.",
