    "This project has no versions yet." : {
      "comment" : "Problem message in the problem list. A version is a version folder in the project."
    },
    "This replaces the whole price schedule. A country not listed here goes back to Apple's equalized price from %@." : {
      "comment" : "Paragraph in the publish plan under the prices of an in-app purchase, shown as fixed-width text. The value is a country code for the base price. A price schedule is a list of prices with start dates."
    },
    "This version refuses some of these changes:\n%@" : {
      "comment" : "Error sentence when a push of text fails. Keep the line break. The value is a list of reasons, one on each line."
    },
    "Translate %@, or silence this warning if the same words in both languages are meant." : {
      "comment" : "Fix in the problem list about an in-app purchase. The value is a field name, such as Name or Description."
    },
    "Translate %@, or silence this warning if the shared text is intentional." : {
      "comment" : "Fix in the problem list about the listing. The value is a field name, such as Subtitle or Keywords."
    },
    "Trim it. App Store Connect keeps the space and counts it." : {
      "comment" : "Fix in the problem list about a text field that starts or ends with a space. The word it refers to the text. Do not translate App Store Connect."
    },
    "Two prices" : {
      "comment" : "Noun. The name of a price curve. A price curve is a set of rules that sets a price in each country. This curve has one price level for richer countries and one for other countries."
    },
    "Two prices per country: the year, and one month of it on a 12-month commitment. Both move by the same factor. Twelve instalments have to come to the price of the year or more. They also have to come to one and a half times it or less." : {
      "comment" : "Paragraph in the publish plan under the prices of a yearly subscription, shown as fixed-width text. Instalments are monthly payments. A factor is a number that the app multiplies the prices by."
    },
    "Use %@ instead." : {
      "comment" : "Fix in the problem list. The value is a language code that App Store Connect accepts."
    },
    "Use %@ instead. App Store Connect uses the three-letter code." : {
      "comment" : "Fix in the problem list. The value is a three-letter country code. Do not translate App Store Connect."
    },
    "Use a 5244x2950 png, or add a search-results file for this language." : {
      "comment" : "How to fix a header that cannot show in search results. Keep search-results as it is: it is a file name."
    },
    "Use a universal link or a link with your app's own scheme, such as myapp://moon." : {
      "comment" : "Fix for a deep link that is not an address. Keep myapp://moon as it is."
    },
    "Use one of: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Fix in the problem list. The value is a list of ids, such as device class ids or price curve ids."
    },
    "Use one of: %@. A company name such as netflix finds one too." : {
      "comment" : "Fix in the problem list. The value is a list of price curve ids. Do not translate netflix. It is a name that the app reads."
    },
    "Use one of: %@. Leave it out for an app on one platform." : {
      "comment" : "Fix in the problem list. The value is a list of platform names, such as ios, macos."
    },
    "Version %@ is %@ and does not accept screenshots." : {
      "comment" : "Reason in the publish plan that screenshots cannot change. The first value is a version number. The second is a state name from App Store Connect, such as IN_REVIEW, or the text an unknown state.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Version %1$@ is %2$@ and does not accept screenshots."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Version %@ is %@ and does not accept screenshots. Add a new version in App Store Connect first." : {
      "comment" : "Reason that the inbox files no screenshots, in the window, the terminal and the MCP tools. The first value is a version number. The second is a state name from App Store Connect, such as READY_FOR_DISTRIBUTION, or the text an unknown state. Do not translate the state name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
